     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">To combat the spread of the COVID-19, and address the adverse socio-economic impacts, UNDP and sister agencies rolled out support anchored on 3 pillars- preparedness, response and recovery. Specifically, this entailed UNDP repurposing program funds worth US$ 2.2 million to strengthen the health system by procuring emergency health care equipment and supplies ; provided social safety nets to vulnerable population in the form of food and cash transfers worth US $500,407 in the Northern Red Sea and Anseba Regions; conducted socio-economic assessment and recovery plan by leveraging on its integrator role and as gatekeeper for the SDGs; provided support for recovery of small enterprises and ensuring workplace safety and well-being of the community; strategic communication by innovating, in cooperation with the Ministry of Health, supported a COVID-19 mobile application for public advocacy &amp; sensitization on prevention and safety measures while fostering youth innovation.</narrative>
